# Expectation record for 03_initializers/010_compound_literals.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 010_compound_literals
area               = 03_initializers
description        = Compound literals in expression, argument, subscript, member-access and sizeof position -- ten forms including a designated literal, a literal nested inside another, by-value and by-address argument passing, an array literal decaying to a pointer, direct subscripting and direct member selection with no intervening variable, and sizeof applied to a literal -- plus a fresh unnamed object per loop iteration, a block-scoped literal read only inside its own block, and the static-duration contrast of two file-scope literals
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour, which is the property both
differential oracles rest on: undefined behaviour would license either compiler to do anything at
all, so a divergence between two compilers over it would prove nothing about either one.
LIFETIME IS THE HAZARD SPECIFIC TO THIS CONSTRUCT, and it is handled explicitly rather than assumed,
because a compound literal is the one initializer form that creates an object in the middle of an
expression. C11 6.5.2.5p5 gives a compound literal appearing at BLOCK scope automatic storage
duration associated with the enclosing block, and one appearing at FILE scope static storage
duration. Every use here respects that.
  - The two literals whose address is taken inside a full expression -- `&(struct pair){ 5, 6 }` and
    the `(int[]){ 10, 20, 30 }` that decays to a pointer in argument position -- are used only for
    the duration of the call, which completes inside that same full expression. Neither pointer
    outlives the object it designates and neither is stored anywhere.
  - The block-scope `(const int[]){ 71, 72, 73 }` is reached through a pointer DECLARED AND READ
    ENTIRELY INSIDE its own braces, so the pointer never escapes the block the object's lifetime is
    tied to. Hoisting that declaration out of the braces would be a genuine use after the object's
    lifetime -- undefined behaviour that would invalidate the oracle rather than test it, and exactly
    what the sanitizer gate is watching for here.
  - Inside the loop, the compound literal's enclosing block is the loop body, so each iteration
    establishes the object afresh from the current value of the counter. Its value is copied
    immediately into the named object `fresh` and NO ADDRESS IS TAKEN there, so the program observes
    the VALUE and never object identity -- which is what keeps the assertion independent of whether
    the implementation reuses one allocation for every iteration.
  - The two file-scope literals have STATIC storage duration, so keeping their addresses and reading
    them at the very end of main -- after every block-scope literal above has expired -- is well
    defined for the whole run.
NO READ TOUCHES UNINITIALIZED STORAGE. A member or element left unmentioned by a brace-enclosed
initializer is initialized as an object of static storage duration would be, that is to zero, for
automatic and static duration alike (C11 6.7.9p19 and p21), and that implicit zeroing applies inside
a compound literal exactly as it does in a declaration: `(struct pair){ .q = 9 }` has p equal to 0
and `(int[4]){ [3] = 64 }` has elements 0 through 2 equal to zero. Those are determinate values
rather than indeterminate ones, and they are part of what is under test rather than merely relied
upon.
No signed overflow is possible. The largest value any expression yields is 506, from p * 100 + q with
p equal to 5 and q equal to 6, and the loop accumulation reaches 9; INT_MAX is at least 2147483647 on
every conforming target. There is no shift, no division and no remainder anywhere in the program.
Every subscript is strictly in bounds: index 0 and index 2 of an int[3] literal, index 1 and index 3
of an int[4] literal, indices 0 through 2 of the three-element block-scope and file-scope array
literals, and indices 0 through 2 inside sum3, whose parameter always receives a three-element array
literal. No one-past-the-end pointer is formed, and every pointer in the program is dereferenced
rather than compared or advanced past its object. No address is printed, so nothing depends on where
the implementation placed an unnamed object.
There is no aliasing violation: every object is read through an lvalue of its own declared type,
which is int in every case, reached by member selection, subscripting or dereference through a
pointer to the matching type. No object representation is inspected, no union appears, no integer-to-
pointer conversion occurs, and the only cast in the program is the `(int)` applied to a sizeof value
of 12 -- a value conversion that cannot change the number. Nothing depends on padding bytes, whose
contents are unspecified, or on the relative addresses of unrelated objects: no pointer difference is
taken and no two addresses are compared.
No object is modified twice between two sequence points. `loop_total += fresh.p + fresh.q;` is a
statement of its own, never embedded in a call, and nothing else in the program assigns at all after
initialization. Every printf call receives at most one loop counter and one already-computed int, and
the three calls that construct a literal as an argument each pass exactly ONE argument whose
evaluation has an effect, so the unspecified order in which a function call's arguments are evaluated
cannot be observed.
Every conversion specifier is %d and every corresponding argument has type int after the default
argument promotions -- the one size is cast to int before reaching the variadic call -- so no
variadic argument is read at the wrong width.
main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is truncated by the
operating system. Every input is a literal in this file: nothing is read from the environment, the
clock, the file system or the network, and iteration order is fixed by literal loop bounds, so every
cell is reproducible from this source and this record alone.
No header is included anywhere and printf is declared by hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`.
bcc bundles the nine required freestanding headers plus a bonus stdatomic.h and ships no standard
I/O header (docs/project-guide.md line 212), so naming one would fail on the bcc side of oracle (a)
while succeeding on the reference side -- a spurious divergence caused by the test rather than by a
compiler. This area is granted no header exception; the corpus has exactly two, area 07's stdarg.h
and the dedicated bundled-header probe in area 12.
This record declares no warning-gate deviation, and area 03 sanctions none. The program is clean
under the full default gate -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow
-Werror at -O0, -O1 and -O2 with all four reference drivers, and it builds and runs clean under the
sanitizer gate -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all. Both gates are
reference-compiler-only and are never applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is
untouched.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This record narrows nothing: all four targets, all three optimization levels and all three
oracles are enabled, no expected-divergence marker is carried, and no `ub_audit_flags` key appears
because the program passes the suite's full default warning gate unmodified.
WIDTH NORMALIZATION. Only int is computed and only %d is printed, so nothing here depends on a type
whose width differs between the four targets: a pointer and the wider integer types were MEASURED at
four bytes on i686 and eight on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64
(docs/technical-specifications.md target table, lines 457-462), and none of them is declared,
computed or printed. The one printed size, cl_sizeof, is sizeof applied to an int[3] rather than to a
pointer, so it is 12 on all four targets, and it is cast to int first so that no size_t reaches the
variadic call.
NO ADDRESS IS EVER PRINTED. Every pointer in the program -- including the one formed by taking the
address of a compound literal, the array literal that decays in argument position, the block-scoped
pointer and the two file-scope pointers -- is dereferenced and its pointee reported instead, so where
the implementation places an unnamed object is unobservable.
PLAIN-CHAR SIGNEDNESS. No character data appears, so the MEASURED split -- signed on x86_64 and
i686, unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64 -- cannot arise.
PADDING AND LAYOUT. Members are read individually by name and no object representation is inspected
and no aggregate is printed whole, so padding, whose contents are unspecified, is never observed.
EXECUTION CHARACTER SET. Nothing character-valued is printed, so C11 5.2.1 leaves nothing here to
the implementation.
THE TWO STORAGE DURATIONS ARE THIS PROGRAM'S VARIANT AXIS, AND THEY TRAVEL DIFFERENT PATHS THROUGH
THE COMPILER FOR THE SAME SYNTAX. A file-scope compound literal has static storage duration and is
resolved into the program's data image at translation time, whereas a block-scope one must be
materialized by emitted code on entry to its block, and the per-iteration literal must be
re-established on every trip round the loop with a value the compiler cannot fold into a single
answer for all three iterations. All three paths are compiled at all three optimization levels.
Passing a literal by value, by address and as an array argument then exercises three distinct ways
the object can reach a callee, which is where a calling-convention difference between the four
backends would surface.
THE TWO-VARIANT STRUCTURE IS A CALL BOUNDARY RATHER THAN A VOLATILE OPERAND, and that choice is
deliberate. take_val, take_ptr and sum3 hold one variant of the computation behind a call that cannot
be folded through at -O0 and is typically inlined at -O2, while the values consumed directly in main
are the other variant, so both the folded and the genuinely computed path are exercised. A volatile
twin is NOT added: the subject here is what a compound literal produces and how long it lives rather
than what an operator computes, the accumulation across the loop already forces real run-time work,
and qualifying an operand would suppress exactly the optimizer behaviour this program exists to
survive.
THE ARGUMENT-PASSING FORMS ARE OBSERVED FROM INSIDE THE CONSUMER, so every member and element that
crossed the parameter-passing boundary carries its own labelled line: take_val_p and take_val_q,
take_ptr_p and take_ptr_q, and sum3_a0, sum3_a1 and sum3_a2. The encoded returns -- take_val_arg=304
and take_ptr_arg=506, both p * 100 + q, and sum3_arg=60 -- remain only as ADDITIONAL cross-checks.
Across forms 4 to 9 that is sixteen directly labelled values: two for each pair-valued literal, three
for the three-element array literal and four for the four-element designated array, so no initialized
slot is represented only by a sum, an encoding or a sampled neighbour. That distinction is the point,
because an encoding or a checksum can be reproduced by two compensating errors -- a swapped pair of
members is the obvious one -- whereas a per-slot line cannot. Comparing take_val_arg against
take_ptr_arg still separates a calling-convention defect from a lifetime defect: one changes and the
other does not. Each consumer call is assigned to a local -- r_take_val, r_take_ptr and r_sum3 --
before the value is printed, so no printf argument carries a side effect. The
directly-subscripted and directly-member-selected forms, which have no intervening variable at all,
are where a compiler that mishandles the unnamed object's address computation or lifetime shows up
first.
MEASURED EVIDENCE. The program was compiled with the reference driver for all four targets at -O0,
-O1 and -O2 -- twelve configurations -- and every one produced these 42 lines byte-identically with
exit status 0, which is why oracle (b) compares this program's targets against each other without any
narrowing and why oracle (c) can hold these bytes as the golden record. Each of the ten forms is read
back on its own line, every one of the sixteen slots that cross a parameter boundary is printed
individually from inside the consumer, and the three encodings named above are redundant
cross-checks rather than substitutes, so a single divergent line localizes the defect to one form.
END
